# Trivy IaC scan suppressions.
# Each entry must carry an expiry date — no silent forever-suppressions.
# Format: AVD-XXX-XXXX exp:YYYY-MM-DD reason:<one line>
#
# Example:
# AVD-AWS-0123 exp:2026-12-31 reason:false positive in node-bootstrap vendor_data template

AVD-AWS-0104 exp:2027-07-07 reason:control-plane-aws/node-pool-aws egress destinations (registry_mirror_url, gitops_*_repo_url) are consumer-supplied and arbitrary, not enumerable at plan time or stable enough to CIDR-scope (CDN-backed hosts). This check only inspects CIDR breadth, not port, so port-scoping cannot clear it. Genuine domain-based egress restriction requires a separate network-layer control (NAT + firewall with FQDN allowlisting) that this module deliberately does not create (CLAUDE.md: never creates network fabric). Unrestricted egress is also the AWS default security-group behavior.

AVD-AZU-0013 exp:2027-07-07 reason:control-plane-azure's Key Vault only ever holds the agent join token, already gated by RBAC (rbac_authorization_enabled = true, Key Vault Secrets Officer/User role assignments) rather than network-level ACL. A default_action = Deny network ACL would block azurerm_key_vault_secret.agent_token's own write during tofu apply, since the applying principal's network (operator laptop, CI runner) isn't knowable at plan time — the same structural issue as AVD-AWS-0104. Worker read access via managed identity would also require the consumer's subnet to have the Microsoft.KeyVault service endpoint enabled, a new prerequisite this module doesn't currently document.
